  {
    "id": "183c884b-18df-5d22-b743-93ef9765b907",
    "pack": "bastion-of-blasphemies",
    "kind": "action",
    "slug": "action:meditate-among-the-stones",
    "name": "Meditate Among the Stones",
    "rarity": "common",
    "traits": ["concentrate", "exploration"],
    "sources": [
      {
        "kind": "book",
        "book": "bastion-of-blasphemies"
      }
    ],
    "description": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "You spend an hour meditating within the ring of standing stones, absorbing the power they contain in an attempt to focus and sharpen your mind. At the end of the hour, attempt a "
          },
          {
            "type": "check",
            "statistic": "save:will",
            "dc": 20
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " save with the following results (this becomes a "
          },
          {
            "type": "check",
            "statistic": "save:will",
            "dc": 25,
            "outcomes": {
              "criticalSuccess": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "Your mind sharpens and your thoughts clear. The next time you attempt an Intelligence-based skill check over the course of the following week, you gain a +2 circumstance bonus to the check."
                }
              ]
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " save if the standing stones haven't been cleared of fungus). Once you Meditate Among the Stones, you cannot attempt to do so again for 1 week, regardless of your results."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "rule"
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Critical Success",
            "marks": ["strong"]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " Your mind sharpens and your thoughts clear. The next time you attempt an Intelligence-based skill check over the course of the following week, you gain a +2 circumstance bonus to the check."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "ref",
            "id": "ce5b89b0-85f4-520f-93a1-7ba3404a3ee6"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Success",
            "marks": ["strong"]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " As critical success, but a +1 circumstance bonus, and the check must be made in the next 24 hours."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "ref",
            "id": "2f476394-e17c-5c43-8488-4f0a3305bcc4"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Failure",
            "marks": ["strong"]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " You meditate and relax, but achieve no enlightenment. If the stones haven't been cleared of fungus, treat this result instead as a critical failure."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Critical Failure",
            "marks": ["strong"]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " As failure, but lingering influence from the Outer Rifts induces unnerving hallucinations that leave you "
          },
          {
            "type": "ref",
            "id": "9e1dad43-36fe-5629-923f-2df63c12d90f",
            "label": "Stupefied 1"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " for 24 hours."
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "rules": [],
    "externalIds": {
      "foundry": "Compendium.pf2e.adventure-specific-actions.Item.j6MnMZ8ADhhEiUTA"
    },
    "data": {
      "category": "interaction"
    }
  },
  {
    "id": "e010f15f-4f22-5692-a4f9-c2abfd2cde78",
    "pack": "bastion-of-blasphemies",
    "kind": "action",
    "slug": "action:play-fatesnatcher",
    "name": "Play Fatesnatcher",
    "rarity": "common",
    "traits": ["concentrate", "exploration"],
    "sources": [
      {
        "kind": "book",
        "book": "bastion-of-blasphemies"
      }
    ],
    "description": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Prophet's Turn:",
            "marks": ["strong"]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " A game of Fatesnatcher plays out over several \"ages.\" During each age, every prophet takes a turn (the PCs can decide in what order they act) by drawing a card from the harrow deck and then using that card as inspiration to spin a fate to Pharasma (Mister Moxie) that catches them by surprise. (At your discretion, you can have the players draw actual harrow cards and use them—if you feel they were particularly creative in coming up with their fate, grant them a +1 circumstance bonus to their skill check to resolve their turn.) The PC then attempts a "
          },
          {
            "type": "check",
            "statistic": "skill:lore:games",
            "dc": 22
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": ", "
          },
          {
            "type": "check",
            "statistic": "skill:deception",
            "dc": 24
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": ", or "
          },
          {
            "type": "check",
            "statistic": "skill:performance",
            "dc": 26,
            "outcomes": {
              "criticalSuccess": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "The PC truly catches Pharasma off-guard. They keep their card and draw a second card from the deck to keep it as a bonus card. Once a PC has collected 10 cards, they win."
                }
              ],
              "success": [{ "type": "text", "text": "The PC catches Pharasma off-guard and keeps their card." }],
              "failure": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "The PC fails to catch Pharasma off-guard. They shuffle their card into the deck and lose 2 omens. If at any point a PC has no omens left, they're out of the game."
                }
              ],
              "criticalFailure": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "The PC fails catastrophically; they shuffle their card into the deck and lose 1d4+1 omens."
                }
              ]
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " check with the following results."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "rule"
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Critical Success",
            "marks": ["strong"]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " The PC truly catches Pharasma off-guard. They keep their card and draw a second card from the deck to keep it as a bonus card. Once a PC has collected 10 cards, they win."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Success",
            "marks": ["strong"]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " The PC catches Pharasma off-guard and keeps their card."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Failure",
            "marks": ["strong"]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " The PC fails to catch Pharasma off-guard. They shuffle their card into the deck and lose 2 omens. If at any point a PC has no omens left, they're out of the game."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Critical Failure",
            "marks": ["strong"]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " The PC fails catastrophically; they shuffle their card into the deck and lose 1d4+1 omens."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "rule"
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Pharasma's Turn:",
            "marks": ["strong"]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " At the end of each age after every prophet has taken their turn, Pharasma grows more fickle. Mister Moxie attempts a "
          },
          {
            "type": "check",
            "statistic": "skill:lore:games",
            "dc": 24,
            "outcomes": {
              "criticalSuccess": [{ "type": "text", "text": "The DCs for all checks to spin a fate increase by 2." }],
              "success": [{ "type": "text", "text": "The DCs for all checks to spin a fate increase by 1." }],
              "failure": [{ "type": "text", "text": "The DCs to spin a fate do not change." }],
              "criticalFailure": [{ "type": "text", "text": "The DCs for all checks to spin a fate decrease by 1." }]
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " check with the following results. After adjusting DCs for the players as appropriate, play proceeds with the next age until all of the prophets have lost their omens or one prophet manages to achieve 10 fates (10 harrow cards)."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "rule"
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Critical Success",
            "marks": ["strong"]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " The DCs for all checks to spin a fate increase by 2."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Success",
            "marks": ["strong"]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " The DCs for all checks to spin a fate increase by 1."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Failure",
            "marks": ["strong"]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " The DCs to spin a fate do not change."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Critical Failure",
            "marks": ["strong"]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " The DCs for all checks to spin a fate decrease by 1."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "rule"
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Losing the Game:",
            "marks": ["strong"]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " The PCs lose the game as soon as all of them are out of omens. In this case, Mister Moxie cackles in delight, his despair at the missing Mushfens Monster forgotten for a few hours, after which he returns to his gloom in the tent. He agrees to play another game of Fatesnatcher with the party after 24 hours have passed, but in the meantime, each PC who played the game must attempt a "
          },
          {
            "type": "check",
            "statistic": "save:will",
            "dc": 24
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " save to avoid becoming "
          },
          {
            "type": "ref",
            "id": "9e1dad43-36fe-5629-923f-2df63c12d90f",
            "label": "Stupefied 1"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " for 24 hours (or for an unlimited duration on a critical failure). This is a curse effect."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Winning the Game:",
            "marks": ["strong"]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " The PCs win the game if any of them ever achieve 10 fates (10 harrow cards) or if at any point during the game there are no harrow cards left to draw (you can ignore this win condition if you're not playing with a real harrow deck for PCs to keep track of their fates). Mister Moxie is surprised but then delighted. He offers the winning PC his harrow deck as a prize."
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "rules": [],
    "externalIds": {
      "foundry": "Compendium.pf2e.adventure-specific-actions.Item.4777eIkPMXyyyqC3"
    },
    "data": {
      "category": "interaction"
    }
  },
  {
    "id": "7163e70d-ce80-54a9-ac82-27af92385a5a",
    "pack": "bastion-of-blasphemies",
    "kind": "action",
    "slug": "action:shelyns-grace",
    "name": "Shelyn's Grace",
    "rarity": "common",
    "traits": ["concentrate", "divine", "healing"],
    "sources": [
      {
        "kind": "book",
        "book": "bastion-of-blasphemies"
      }
    ],
    "description": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
